#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:338
#: 8246f66cc38f4e39a815448813f53a8d
msgid "Xen PV drivers and Qubes Windows Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:341
#: 408cc76e98b04b088cf790e9f7b5934f
msgid ""
"Installing Xen’s PV drivers in the VM will lower its resources usage when "
"using network and/or I/O intensive applications, but *may* come at the price "
"of system stability (although Xen’s PV drivers on a Windows VM are usually "
"very stable). They can be installed as an optional part of Qubes Windows "
"Tools (QWT), which bundles Xen’s PV drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:343
#: 5303abcdd77e4ac7947d692a110c1499
msgid "**Notes** about using Xen’s VBD (storage) PV driver:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:345
#: 59d5258548da458ba21cd81104c29230
msgid ""
"**Windows 7:** Installing the driver requires a fully updated VM, or else "
"you’ll likely get a BSOD (“Blue Screen Of Death”) and a VM in a difficult-to-"
"fix state. Updating Windows takes *hours* and for casual usage there isn’t "
"much of a performance between the disk PV driver and the default one; so "
"there is likely no need to go through the lengthy Windows Update process if "
"your VM doesn’t have access to untrusted networks and if you don’t use I/O "
"intensive apps or attach block devices. If you plan to update your newly "
"installed Windows VM, it is recommended that you do so *before* installing "
"Qubes Windows Tools. Installing the driver will probably cause Windows 7 "
"activation to become invalid, but the activation can be restored using the "
"Microsoft telephone activation method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:347
#: cbe86b5b890742fbaa39e5582cb19451
msgid ""
"The option to install the storage PV driver is disabled by default in Qubes "
"Windows Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:349
#: 24f3fabdb89445c0a02285e1df488fb1
msgid ""
"In case you already had QWT installed without the storage PV driver and you "
"then updated the VM, you may then install the driver by again starting the "
"QWT installer and selecting the change option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:354
#: eaaa13bf181e4b948ae8d83170a013bc
msgid "Using Windows AppVMs in seamless mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:357
#: 9a752f0e2cb14a10beb71ce20a43b9ed
msgid ""
"Windows Apps can be started using the Qubes menu. Alternatively, you can "
"open the Windows menu by typing the Windows key on your keyboard while the "
"cursor is positioned in a window of the Windows VM."
msgstr ""

