msgid ""
"When we publish a new QWT version, it’s usually pushed to the ``current-"
"testing`` or ``unstable`` repository first. To use versions from current-"
"testing, run this in dom0:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:635
#: ab6554b1f8204c798988d8f9e8c2336b
msgid ""
"That command will download a new QWT ``iso`` file from the testing "
"repository. It goes without saying that you should **backup your VMs** "
"before installing anything from testing repos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:639
#: d1306e1ce2164f0aa3dc30eb77c6d3b9
msgid "Uninstalling Qubes Windows Tools in a Windows VM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:645
#: 3a439075f2df487eb168b634a726f27c
msgid ""
"Uninstall QWT 4.1.69-1, using the standard procedure from the system control "
"panel of Windows. This will most likely result in a crash with the error "
"INACCESSIBLE BOOT DEVICE, especially if the PV drivers were installed with "
"QWT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:647
#: 185fd08e85a746898c295aeda6e5f073
msgid ""
"Restart Windows again, hitting the :kbd:`F8` key, select the restart menu, "
"and then select a start in safe mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:649
#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:670
#: 13823c3d12724fa2bf1307fafa762856 66e7cce819b846e4b0d4a16db4ed0151
msgid ""
"The system will start again, but in a rather useless way. Just shut it down "
"and reboot again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:651
#: 5f68880be8d54e21b83fb5c6c781627b
msgid ""
"Now Windows will start normally. Check within the control panel if there are "
"any Xen drivers left. If so, uninstall them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:653
#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:674
#: f5ffc6b52b3646e7833106f7d23c0deb e8bc691a3fd3468c8962f904db60fc48
msgid ""
"In the Windows device manager, check if there is still a (probably non-"
"working) Xen PV disk device. If so, uninstall it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:655
#: 32de1d1fccad4301b39c397c67dd141e
msgid ""
"In the control panel, check again if the Xen drivers are removed. A Xen Bus "
"Package (version 8.2.1.8) may remain and cannot be removed, but does no "
"harm. Any other Xen drivers should have disappeared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:659
#: face2229650246a1843d1184069ae5b9
msgid "Windows 10 and 11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:662
#: 9e87f676a9a747a19c6b58ca3e44c7db
msgid ""
"If there is a drive ``D:`` from this earlier installation of Qubes Windows "
"Tools, it will probably contain incomplete private data; especially the "
"folder ``AppData`` containing program configuration data will be missing. In "
"this situation, it may be better to perform a new Windows installation, "
"because repair may be difficult and trouble-prone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:664
#: 9654f2488bbf48a9a70b84b094e166a9
msgid ""
"First, be sure that the automatic repair function is disabled. In a command "
"window, execute ``bcdedit /set recoveryenabled NO``, and check that this "
"worked by issuing the command ``bcdedit``, without parameters, again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:666
#: bb70be5323ac4c15844ce2db16935f6b
msgid ""
"Now, uninstall QWT (currently version 4.2.2-1), using the Apps and Features "
"function of Windows. This will most likely result in a crash with the error "
"INACCESSIBLE BOOT DEVICE, especially if the PV drivers were installed with "
"QWT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:668
#: 679f5141ca8643109272a51ddb6de81c
msgid ""
"Restart Windows again, possibly two or three times, until repair options are "
"offered. By hitting the F8 key, select the restart menu, and in that menu "
"select a start in safe mode (in German, it’s option number 4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:672
#: e8b0fd267ba540e6af44ad0c71977b0d
msgid ""
"Now Windows will start normally. Check in the Apps and Features display if "
"there are any Xen drivers left. If so, uninstall them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:676
#: a5e7f2bbe091409cba5675b8557b13ca
msgid ""
"In the Apps and Features display, check again if the Xen drivers are "
"removed. A Xen Bus Package may remain and cannot be removed, but it does not "
"cause harm. Any other Xen drivers should have disappeared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:678
#: f1805da989714b2e9cd5e15f8a09c149
msgid ""
"In order to avoid Qubes stopping Windows VMs forcefully after QWT was "
"uninstalled, it is advisable to undefine the qrexec control for these VMs. "
"This can be done using the command ``qvm-features <VMNAME> qrexec \"\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:680
#: fa7ab250250648308b116ed5851831e6
msgid ""
"After successful uninstallation of the PV disk drivers, the disks will "
"appear as QEMU ATA disks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:682
#: 7b0a6b38b32943e1ac0286a7701428cf
msgid ""
"**Warning:** The uninstallation of the PV disk drivers may lead Windows to "
"declare that the hardware has changed and that, in consequence, the "
"activation is no longer valid, possibly complaining that the use of the "
"software is no longer lawful. It should be possible to reactivate the "
"software if a valid product key is provided."
msgstr ""
